  - evidence_type: RECIPE_SOURCE
    source: https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium135.pdf
    source_record: DSMZ 135/339a sodium carbonate 5% w/v stock
    notes: Printed solute identity and stock strength are retained; no stock-specific
      carrier is stated. Child reference_scope UNMAPPED means no exact child identifier
      was independently established.
  notes: Both DSMZ 135 and 339a specify sterile, anoxic 5% w/v Na2CO3 stock prepared
    under 80% N2 / 20% CO2 for pH adjustment. Dissolved-gas amounts and speciation
    are not quantified. Neither source names this stock carrier; w/v defines mass
    per solution volume, not solvent identity. Explicit in-H2O wording for a different
    phenosafranin stock does not transfer. Stock solvent identity and grade, carbonate
    crystal hydrate and complete preparation remain unknown. This stock is not exact
    identity with pure Na2CO3, and the unspecified-basis ATCC 1612 5% stock is not
    automatically included.
notes: 'Both DSMZ 135 and 339a specify sterile, anoxic 5% w/v Na2CO3 stock prepared
  under 80% N2 / 20% CO2 for pH adjustment. Dissolved-gas amounts and speciation are
  not quantified. Neither source names this stock carrier; w/v defines mass per solution
  volume, not solvent identity. Explicit in-H2O wording for a different phenosafranin
  stock does not transfer. Stock solvent identity and grade, carbonate crystal hydrate
  and complete preparation remain unknown. This stock is not exact identity with pure
  Na2CO3, and the unspecified-basis ATCC 1612 5% stock is not automatically included.
  Raw source labels retained without global resolving aliases: ["Na2CO3 (5% w/v)"].
  Occurrence-specific linkage is required; identical generic words in other recipes
  do not imply the same formulation.'
